
# Assignment 3.4 — Semantic HTML & Accessibility

## 1. Objective

To convert a div-based webpage into a semantic HTML webpage using elements such as `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<article>`, `<aside>`, and `<footer>`. The goal is to improve webpage structure, readability, accessibility, and maintainability.

## 2. Before: Div-Based HTML

The following is an example of a webpage that uses only `<div>` elements for its structure.

Save this code as `before.html`.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>My Portfolio</title>
</head>
<body>

    <div>
        <h1>My Portfolio</h1>
    </div>

    <div>
        <a href="index.html">Home</a>
        <a href="about.html">About</a>
        <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
    </div>

    <div>
        <div>
            <h2>About Me</h2>
            <p>Hello! I am a web development student learning HTML and CSS.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h2>My Skills</h2>
            <p>I am learning HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Git.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
            <h3>Useful Resource</h3>
            <p>Visit the MDN website to learn more about web development.</p>
            <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/"
               target="_blank"
               rel="noopener noreferrer">MDN Web Docs</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div id="contact">
        <h2>Contact Me</h2>
        <p>Email: example@email.com</p>
    </div>

    <div>
        <p>Copyright 2026 My Portfolio.</p>
    </div>

</body>
</html>
```

## 3. After: Semantic HTML

Create a file named `index.html` and use the following improved code.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My Portfolio - Semantic HTML</title>
</head>
<body>

    <header>
        <h1>My Portfolio</h1>
        <p>Welcome to my personal portfolio website.</p>
    </header>

    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <ul>
            <li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="#about">About</a></li>
            <li><a href="#skills">Skills</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>

    <main>
        <section id="about">
            <h2>About Me</h2>
            <p>
                Hello! I am a web development student learning HTML and CSS.
                I enjoy creating webpages and learning new technologies.
            </p>

            <img
                src="images/profile.jpg"
                alt="Profile photograph for my personal portfolio"
                width="200"
                height="200">
        </section>

        <section id="skills">
            <h2>My Skills</h2>

            <article>
                <h3>HTML</h3>
                <p>
                    HTML helps me create the structure and content of webpages.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>CSS</h3>
                <p>
                    CSS helps me style webpages using colors, spacing, and layouts.
                </p>
            </article>

            <article>
                <h3>JavaScript</h3>
                <p>
                    JavaScript helps me add interactivity to webpages.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <aside>
            <h2>Useful Resource</h2>
            <p>
                Learn more about web development using the MDN Web Docs website.
            </p>
            <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/"
               target="_blank"
               rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Visit MDN Web Docs
            </a>
        </aside>

        <section id="contact">
            <h2>Contact Me</h2>
            <p>Email: example@email.com</p>
            <p>You can contact me for questions about my projects.</p>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 My Portfolio. All rights reserved.</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>
```

Note: Create an `images` folder and add your own profile image named `profile.jpg`. If you do not want to include an image, you can remove the `<img>` element.

## 4. Explanation of Semantic HTML Elements

1. `<header>`: Contains the introductory content or heading of the page.
2. `<nav>`: Contains navigation links to other pages or sections.
3. `<main>`: Contains the main content of the webpage.
4. `<section>`: Groups related content into meaningful sections.
5. `<article>`: Contains independent content, such as an individual skill description.
6. `<aside>`: Contains related supplementary information, such as useful resources.
7. `<footer>`: Contains copyright information or other footer content.
8. `alt`: Provides a meaningful description of an image for screen readers and when the image cannot load.

## 5. Heading Hierarchy

The webpage uses headings in a logical order:

- `<h1>`: My Portfolio
- `<h2>`: About Me, My Skills, Useful Resource, Contact Me
- `<h3>`: HTML, CSS, JavaScript

This hierarchy makes the page easier to understand and navigate.

## 6. Accessibility Improvements

- Navigation links are placed inside the `<nav>` element.
- Main content is placed inside `<main>`.
- Sections have meaningful headings and unique IDs.
- The profile image includes descriptive alternative text.
- Links use understandable text instead of vague labels.
- The external link uses `rel="noopener noreferrer"` with `target="_blank"`.
- The document includes a language attribute and a responsive viewport setting.

